<title>FRANCE: French mobile telephone use up 5.8 percent in July.</title>
<headline>French mobile telephone use up 5.8 percent in July.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The number of subscriptions to mobile telecommunications services increased by 5.8 percent to 1,813,200 in July, according to France's general directorate of post and telecommunications.</p>
<p>France Telecom's Itineris had a 5.9 percent increase to 992,500, Generale des Eaux SFR unit had a 8.4 percent increase to 541,600 while Bouygues Telecom had a 74 percent rise to 22,100 in its second month of operation.</p>
<p>Itineris had the biggest absolute rise -- 55,200 in July and 269,300 over the past six months.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
